To solve the problem of finding duplicates in a list while maintaining the order of their first appearance, we can use a combination of a dictionary to track occurrences and a list to store the duplicates. The dictionary will help us count how many times each item appears in the list, and the list will ensure that we only add an item to the duplicates list once, even if it appears multiple times in the input list.

