To create a React Native FlatList with a fixed-height row of 60 pixels, I will use the `getItemLayout` prop to optimize performance by providing the list with pre-calculated layout information for each item. This is particularly useful when the items have a consistent height, as it allows the FlatList to skip measuring the layout of each item, which can improve rendering efficiency, especially for large lists. Additionally, I will ensure that the data passed to the FlatList is an array of objects, each representing a row, and that the renderItem function correctly displays each item based on this data structure.

ANSWER:

```javascript
import React from 'react';
import { FlatList, View, Text } from 'react-native';

const DATA = Array.from({ length: 100 }, (_, index) => ({ id: index, title: `Item ${index}` }));

const Item = ({ title }) => (
  <View style={{ height: 60, justifyContent: 'center', padding: 16 }}>
    <Text>{title}</Text>
  </View>
);

const App = () => {
  const getItemLayout = (data, index) => ({
    length: 60,
    offset: 60 * index,
    index,
  });

  return (
    <FlatList
      data={DATA}
      renderItem={({ item }) => <Item title={item.title} />}
      keyExtractor={item => item.id.toString()}
      getItemLayout={getItemLayout}
    />
  );
};

export default App;
```

